# listend live DB ingest contract

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

## Parse → write stage (mandatory)

- **Two-stage pipeline (same as sync_timedb):** host-affine **parse** threads (`listend-db-N`) produce post-delta host/proc **dataframes** via ``ingest_monitor_sample_text`` (`sync_timedb_sample_ingest.py`); process-wide **write** threads (`sync_timedb_ingest_write_stage`) COPY/upsert via ``_write_stats_payload_to_db``. Parse threads must **not** open ingest DB write sessions or call host ``bulk_create``.
- **Pool lifecycle:** ``ListendDbIngestPool.start`` / ``stop`` call ``start_ingest_write_stage`` / ``stop_ingest_write_stage`` with ``process_title="listend.py"``. Write width / queue depth reuse **sync** INI only: ``get_sync_ingest_write_pool_processes()`` and ``get_sync_ingest_parse_queue_max()``. Do **not** add ``listend_db_ingest_write_*`` knobs.
- **Flush:** pending frames → COPY ``bytes`` on ``IngestWritePayload`` + blocking ``submit_ingest_write_and_wait`` (``_submit_listend_write_frames``). A failed COPY does not INSERT and does not set ``emit=insert``; the archived sample stays for sync_timedb. Poison flush errors and COPY failures drop the batch; transient errors retain pending frames for retry. Live listend still never writes the file-complete mark.
- **statement_timeout:** apply ``listend_db_ingest_statement_timeout_ms`` on write workers via ``worker_setup=_apply_listend_db_ingest_statement_timeout`` (not on parse threads). Proc peak-merge / dedupe / COPY live on the shared write path — not listend-private flush helpers.

## Invariants

- **File durable when consuming; DB backpressure mode is INI-selected.** RabbitMQ ack only after successful archive append (on a **host-affine archive worker thread**, not the AMQP callback). Competing AMQP consumers (**`listend_amqp_consumer_count`**, default **16**, floor **1**, no upper clamp) each own one pika ``BlockingConnection`` on the original ingest queue (no in-process router, no `{queue}.listend.{i}` shards). Consume thread: pause-check → cheap host+unix-second+``$`` peek (`parse_monitor_payload_archive_hint` / `parse_host_from_monitor_payload`: skip leading ASCII whitespace — monitor samples start with `\\n` before `timestamp jobid host` — then first sample line `split(None, 3)`, or first two lines when that prefix starts with `$`; AMQP **bytes**, no full-body decode/`str.split`/`bytes.lstrip()` of the remainder) → enqueue `_ArchiveWorkItem` (originating session, delivery_tag, payload, host, ts, `$`) on archive queue `adler32(host)%N` (**2 × `listend_amqp_consumer_count`**, default **32**). When **N>1**, the archive worker heap-sorts per host by `(unix_second, $ before digit)` with a **1.0s** hold; **N=1** skips reorder (single-connection FIFO). Missing ts flushes immediately. Archive worker: durable append of raw AMQP bytes → **that item’s** `connection.add_callback_threadsafe(basic_ack)` → best-effort `submit_listend_db_ingest` (held archive fd + byte range after ack; no full-sample decode on the submit path). **Forbid** using process-global `set_amqp_connection` as the ack target when N>1 (406 unknown delivery tag). Sample writes reuse a kept O_APPEND fd and sticky `{current}.fnctl.lock` (`LOCK_EX` only around the write; do not unlink the sidecar every sample; do not change `file_write_lock` for tar callers). `$` rotate caches the digit-epoch path/inode so a same-inode hit skips `scandir`. Archive I/O failure → threadsafe nack+requeue on the originating connection. When live ingest is on and DB queues hit the **high watermark** (module constants **0.95** of total byte budget, or any host-affine worker cannot accept another min-floor payload), behavior follows **`[PIPELINE] listend_db_ingest_backpressure`** (`get_listend_db_ingest_backpressure()`, default **`drop`**):
  - **`drop`** — still archive + ack; live enqueue fails closed and increments `queue_drops`; consume continues. Prefer this when broker buffering is undesirable. Apply **`basic_qos(prefetch_count=listend_amqp_prefetch)`** per consumer (default **32**; process-wide unacked = **32×N**; 16 consumers → **512**).
  - **`pause`** — nack+requeue **without** archive, `stop_consuming`, wait until usage ≤ **resume watermark 0.50** (and every worker has min-floor headroom) while pumping heartbeats. Overflow stays on the broker ready queue. `basic_qos(prefetch_count=1)` **per consumer** only when live on **and** mode is `pause`.
  Watermark fractions remain **module constants** in `listend_db_ingest.py` (not INI). Master switch `listend_db_ingest_enabled=no` (default **no**; opt-in `= yes`) disables live DB entirely.
- **Live-DB enqueue — in-process `queue.Queue`.** After durable archive, `submit` opens `archive_path` `O_RDONLY` and enqueues `(host, fd, offset, length, size)` (`size=length`) on the host-affine worker's `queue.Queue`. The worker `os.pread`s the range, UTF-8-decodes with `errors=replace`, then `os.close`s the fd. Workers are dedicated **threads** (not spawn Processes). There is **no** POSIX SharedMemory, **no** `/dev/shm` `hps-ld-*` segment, and **no** full-sample string copy on the queue. Missing path / open failure / over-budget / `queue.Full` → `queue_drops` (already-acked; never nack). Disabled pool (`listend_db_ingest_enabled=no`) does not start threads. Compose **`pipeline.shm_size`** is leftover spawn IPC for other daemons (modest **1g**), not a listend payload requirement.
- **`$` rotate hardlinks are unique inodes.** Digit epoch filenames must not share a path with a **different** inode. `_ensure_current_hardlinked_to_timestamp` / new-current `os.link` pick an unused digit name (decrement below rotate-wall cutoff for the pre-unlink safety link; for the new `current`, start at the **first plausible sample unix second in the newly written file**, then **+1** on name conflict; fall back to `int(time.time())` only when the `$` payload has no sample timestamp). **Never** `os.remove` an epoch path that is a different inode (same-second double `$` would delete the just-closed segment). Any samefile digit name is durable enough to unlink `current`. `_get_first_timestamp_seconds` skips `$` schema host lines (`1 <fqdn>`); only plausible unix seconds (`>= 1e9`) name files. Name collision is recoverable — ack after a unique link, do not nack/requeue. Real I/O (`ENOSPC`, `EACCES`, empty `current` with no timestamp) still fail-closed nack.
- **Never insert incomplete samples.** `host_data` uniqueness / itimes / duplicate-scan use **host + unix-second**. Any row for second `T` without the full event set from that monitor sample makes sync_timedb treat `T` as done → **permanent silent loss** under `ignore_conflicts`. Live path: whole-sample skip without schema (or with schema mismatch / parse failure); no per-type silent drops like the file parser.
- **Host-affine workers** (`hash(host) % N`, stable adler32): per-host `schema_by_host` + `DeltaCarryState`. `$` updates schema; cold-start may seed from on-disk `current` `!` lines. Carry survives `bulk_create` flush; schema/carry not cleared on flush. Archive threads use the **same** adler32 affine index over **2 × `listend_amqp_consumer_count`**. **Liveness:** if a `listend-db-N` `Thread.is_alive()` is false, log ERROR and **respawn the same index on the same queue** (`ensure_workers_alive`). Do **not** use `ps` argv or Linux `comm` for liveness (`setthreadtitle` is not process argv; `comm` is 15-char). No double-start of a living thread.
- **Batch size / bounded flush** — `listend_db_ingest_batch_samples` (default 100) is an **upper bound** on samples. `$` does not count toward batch. Also flush when pending frame rows reach **`listend_db_ingest_flush_max_rows`** (default **2000**) or when pending has been held for **`listend_db_ingest_flush_hold_s`** (default **5** s) even if the shard queue is never empty (idle `queue.get` Empty never fires at a GiB cap). Policy lives in `_should_flush_pending`. Flush on those triggers, idle timeout, or shutdown → write stage. **Do not** emit per-flush INFO. Record successful flush rows/elapsed on `_FlushWindowStats`; the 10-minute idle-monitor line reports **`flush_rows_avg=`**, **`flush_rows_max=`**, **`flush_elapsed_avg_s=`**, **`flush_elapsed_max_s=`** (then reset). Keep ERROR on flush failure. Proc dedupe / peak-merge / COPY are owned by the shared write path (`insert_proc_data_batch` / `_write_stats_payload_to_db`); listend must not reintroduce private `bulk_create` flush. **`listend_db_ingest_proc_peak_lookup_chunk`** still sizes shared peak-merge lookups when the write path uses it. **host_proc parse:** strip `@fast`/`@full` like host_data; `@fast` uses `schema_fast` (slow keys stay `None`); always `schema_key_basename` on `!host_proc` tokens (`,U=kB`, `,R=S`, …).
- **Queue budget** — `listend_db_ingest_queue_max_gb` (default 8 GiB) total across **parse** workers; **hard-capped at 8 GiB** in the getter and `compute_listend_db_queue_budgets` (INI 12 cannot recreate a 12 GiB copy budget; pool start logs once when clipped). Byte tracker is authoritative; Queue `maxsize` is derived from budget ÷ min payload floor. The budget sizes parse-debt + held fds, not 3 MiB × N copied sample strings. Write-stage slot backpressure uses sync ``sync_ingest_parse_queue_max``.
- **Connection recycle** — write-stage workers own Django DB sessions (same as sync). Parse threads must not recycle write connections. Idle `queue.Empty` still flushes pending frames to the write stage.
- **BLAS/OpenMP caps** — each parse thread must call `configure_blas_thread_env()` before importing numpy/pandas (`sync_timedb_parsing` / sample ingest), or 32 threads × default OpenBLAS threads hit `pthread_create` EAGAIN. Process-once at `listend` start is also sufficient if it happens before any thread imports parsing.
- **Django bootstrap once, on the starting thread** — `ListendDbIngestPool.start()` calls `configure_blas_thread_env()` then `ensure_django()` **before** starting the write stage or any parse thread; a failed bootstrap propagates out of `start()` (listend logs one `Failed to start listend db ingest pool`) instead of killing every worker. `django.setup()` is **not** thread-safe. Parse workers still call `ensure_django()` (idempotent) for side-mark flush; write workers apply ``listend_db_ingest_statement_timeout_ms`` via ``worker_setup``. Regression: `test_django_bootstrap.py`, `test_pool_start_bootstraps_django_before_worker_threads`, `test_pool_start_propagates_django_bootstrap_failure`, `test_listend_pool_wires_sync_write_stage`.
- **Strict post-use memory release** — drop message/DataFrame refs after parse; clear pending frame lists after successful or poison write-stage flush; reuse `release_spawn_pool_worker_memory` cadence on flush/idle (not every sample). Run **memory-leak review** before close when changing this path.
- **When `listend_db_ingest_enabled`:** sync_timedb must **not** use weak `_try_db_complete_head_tail_fast_path` / `_try_db_complete_tail_window_fast_path`. Fall through to duplicate-timestamp scan (`db_skip=full_scan` when all sample seconds present). Archive/delete gate requires **sync_timedb file-complete mark** (or zero-host mark for proc-only) — never live-only head+tail. Live listend **never** writes the file-complete mark.
- Process titles: `listend.py [main]` / `listend.py [thread:amqp-consumer-N]` / `listend.py [thread:listend-db-N]` / `listend.py [thread:ingest-write-pool]` (write stage; same role label as sync) / `listend.py [thread:archive-N]`. Extend the existing 10-minute idle monitor with DB counters (`pause_enters`, `pause_s`, `paused`, `db_queued_bytes`, `queue_drops`) plus **`alive_db_threads=`**, **`max_shard_qsize=`**, **`max_shard_bytes=`**, **`flush_rows_avg=`**, **`flush_rows_max=`**, **`flush_elapsed_avg_s=`**, **`flush_elapsed_max_s=`** (window avg/max of successful flush rows and elapsed, then reset). `format_idle_monitor_suffix()` calls `ensure_workers_alive()` so the 10-minute line also heals dead shards. Archive suffix is **`archive_q_depth=`** plus **`inflight=`** (busy workers + reorder-held) and **`amqp_consumers=`** / **`prefetch=`** (per-consumer QoS). Report backpressure pause **duration** on that idle line only — **no** per-transition INFO on the consume wait loop when pausing or resuming RabbitMQ consume (or re-logging `Begining Consume` on pause-resume rebind). Do **not** start 32 parse workers per AMQP thread.
- **AMQP channel/connection death during consume/ack:** treat as **connection-scoped** failure (not process-global when N>1). Detect closed/closing channel/connection (message text including `closed or closing connection` and 406 `unknown delivery tag` / `PRECONDITION_FAILED`, pika wrong-state / stream-lost / AMQP channel errors, or `channel.is_closed` / `connection.is_closed` / `is_closing`). `_request_amqp_full_reconnect` sets the **session** reconnect flag (throttled log) and must **not** close sibling consumers. That session’s I/O thread then `stop_consuming` + `channel.close()` then `connection.close()`. Archive / non-I/O-thread callers must **never** close or `stop_consuming` (pika `BlockingConnection` is **not thread-safe**); they schedule that teardown via `add_callback_threadsafe` on **that item’s connection** when it still looks open, and skip when it is already closed/closing (`add_callback_threadsafe` on a dead connection raises `ConnectionWrongStateError`). Skip ack/nack scheduling when that consume connection is already closed/closing or reconnect is already requested. Each `_AmqpConsumeSession.bind` bumps generation. The generation used for ack/nack is the value captured when the message is enqueued (`_ArchiveWorkItem.ack_generation`); a later `bind` must not `basic_ack` that tag on the new channel. Deferred ack/nack callbacks still no-op when that session’s generation/connection changed after the callback was scheduled, so leftover tags cannot 406 on the next channel. Each consumer’s outer `while True` rebuilds a new BlockingConnection after exponential backoff. Do **not** emit per-message `Error processing message; leaving on server: Channel is closed.` spam. Unacked work stays on the broker for redelivery after reconnect. **Pause/resume** (`_db_backpressure_pause`) remains same-connection and must **not** set the session reconnect flag. Idle-monitor waiting count prefers management HTTP ``messages_ready`` then a **separate short-lived** AMQP connection (do not merge with the N consumer connections). Client **`frame_max=131072`** (`LISTEND_AMQP_FRAME_MAX`, RabbitMQ default) plus broker `services-conf/rabbitmq_frame_max.conf`. Do not raise ``pika.spec.FRAME_MAX_SIZE``. Log per-consumer prefetch and negotiated `frame_max` at consume start. Stagger first `basic_consume` (~0.5s × index) to limit quorum 541.
- **Durable monitor ingest queues default to quorum on create** (compose `default_queue_type = quorum`; classic OOMs under many AMQP publishers). `hpcperfstats.lib.rmq_quorum_queue.declare_durable_quorum_queue` **passive-attaches** when the named queue already exists (any type — never send `x-queue-type=quorum` against an existing queue; that 406 closes the channel). Missing queues are created durable quorum. Callers **must assign the returned channel** (404/406 close the original). Do **not** convert an existing queue to classic from listend. Broker `INTERNAL_ERROR` 541 (including bare `(541, 'INTERNAL_ERROR')`) “timed out consuming from quorum queue” is consume-setup/Ra checkout failure — log as quorum consume-setup (not only “establishing connection”), skip `cancel()` before the first `basic_consume` on a fresh channel, exponential reconnect backoff (5→10→20… cap 60s) for **541, peer reset (`ConnectionResetError`/stream lost), and AMQP handshake timeout**. Reset backoff only after **stable consume ≥30s** (`AMQP_RECONNECT_STABLE_CONSUME_SECONDS`), not on `Begining Consume` alone. Graceful reconnect teardown: `stop_consuming` → `channel.close()` → `connection.close()` to reduce broker `channel_termination_timeout` under load. Mass broker `heartbeat_send_error` + listend `channel_termination_timeout` ⇒ broker capacity/teardown race — keep quorum; do not convert to classic. Idle-monitor waiting count prefers management HTTP **`messages_ready`** (same as `rabbitmqctl list_queues`); AMQP `queue.declare-ok.message_count` is **0** for quorum queues with consumers. Passive AMQP remains fallback on a separate short-lived connection. Probe failure must log **`waiting=n/a`** (not `0`).
- **`host_data.jid` from sample header:** digit-line jobid must propagate on stats tags through `compute_deltas_and_arc*` collapse (`"first"` within the group; not a group key) into `host_data.jid`. Idle `-` maps to NULL at ORM (`host_data_instance_from_stats_row`). Same contract for archive `sync_timedb` (shared `sync_timedb_parsing`).

